 61CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2013Sc06:                          
 61CU2c  Phys Rev C 87, 034306 (2013); and 2013ScZZ:                            
 61CU3c  Submission to XUNDL database, March 14, 2013                           
 61CU c  Compiled by E. Thiagalingam and B. Singh (McMaster), May 12, 2013      
 61CU c  Proton adding reactions                                                
 61CU c  E({+3}He)=18 MeV, E(|a)=38 MeV from Yale tandem accelerator of WNSL    
 61CU2c  facility. Measured deuteron, triton spectra, |s(|q), spectroscopic     
 61CU3c  factor C{+2}S using a split-pole spectrograph. FWHM |?50 keV for       
 61CU4c  deuterons and |?64 keV for tritons. Target=204 |mg/cm{+2} thick, 99.7% 
 61CU5c  enriched. Deduced levels, J, |p. DWBA analysis.                        
 61CU6c  Comparison with shell-model calculations.                              
 61CU c  The uncertainties are estimated to be |?4% for |s>1 mb/sr, |?7% for    
 61CU2c  0.1<|s< 1.0 mb/sr, and |?18% for |s< 0.1 mb/sr at their respective     
 61CU3c  maxima. The uncertainties arising from possible contaminants or        
 61CU4c  previously unidentified states for very weak transitions could be      
 61CU5c  |?0.02 mb/sr.                                                          
